      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is the best app for health and safety site inspection reports in the UK?</h3><p>There is no single best. Mitti (formerly SafetyCulture) suits one wide platform, Notify suits a full H&amp;S management system, GoAudits and Lumiform suit checklist audits priced per user, SIAPP suits one person pinning photos to floor plans, and Quickler suits teams whose hours go on the write-up: you answer in WhatsApp and the report is written in your own layout.</p><h3>Do I need an app for site inspection reports?</h3><p>No. The law asks for inspections and, in some cases, a written report. It does not ask for software. Paper works. An app helps when reports are slow to write, hard to find, or filled in later from memory.</p><h3>How much time can an inspection app save?</h3><p>Graeme Clark, an H&amp;S consultant at Ethos Safety, went from 1 to 2 hours of write-up per report to 14 minutes on average. Most of that time was typing after the visit, not the inspection itself.</p><h3>What must a site safety inspection report include under CDM 2015?</h3><p>CDM 2015 requires a written report when the inspector of an excavation or cofferdam is not satisfied that work can be done safely (regulation 24), and the Work at Height Regulations 2005 require one for working platform inspections (regulation 12 and Schedule 7). For a general walk round, record the site, date and time, who inspected, what was checked, what was found and any action. Check current HSE guidance for your work.</p><h3>How often are site safety inspections needed?</h3><p>It depends on the work and risk. A working platform used for construction work, from which a person could fall 2 metres or more, must not be used unless it has been inspected in position within the previous 7 days (Work at Height Regulations 2005, regulation 12). It must also be inspected after installation and after events that may have affected it. General site inspections are often weekly. The principal contractor's risk assessment sets it.</p><h3>Can I do a site safety inspection on a phone?</h3><p>Yes. What matters is doing it on site, during the inspection, not afterwards. WhatsApp has nothing to install and no login.</p><h3>Who can carry out a CDM site safety inspection?</h3><p>Inspections the Regulations require, such as those of excavations and working platforms, must be made by a competent person. That means someone with enough knowledge of the hazards on that site. Check current HSE guidance.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/near-miss-reporting-construction-uk.html\">Near miss reporting in construction</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/risk-assessment-software-uk-sme.html\">Risk assessment software for UK SMEs</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/h-and-s-site-walkround-checklist-uk.html\">H&S site walkround checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/coshh-risk-assessment-field-teams-uk.html\">COSHH risk assessment for field teams</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a></li></ul>"
